  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels:\n\n\\[\n7 \\text{ shrimp/minute} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}=70\\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nSince 70 is less than the 100 shrimp available, she can peel and sauté:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{70}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\text{ shrimp/minute} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}=60\\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nSince 60 is less than the 100 shrimp available, she can peel and sauté:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{60}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60 \\text{ shrimp}\n\\]\n\nShe discards 5 damaged shrimp afterward:\n\n\\[\n60-5=55\n\\]\n\nSo Emily peels \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp, of which \\(\\boxed{55}\\) remain usable.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "In ten minutes, Emily can:\n\n- Peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp.\n- Keep \\(60-5=55\\) usable shrimp after discarding 5.\n- Sauté \\(\\frac{30}{12}\\times 10=25\\) shrimp.\n\nTherefore, the number she can both peel and sauté in ten minutes is limited by her sautéing rate:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "In 10 minutes, Emily can:\n\n- Peel \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\) shrimp.\n- Discard 5 damaged shrimp, leaving \\(60-5=55\\) usable shrimp.\n- Sauté 30 shrimp.\n\nThus, she can both peel and sauté:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30\\text{ shrimp}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Emily peels and sautés each shrimp sequentially:\n\n- Peeling takes \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) minute per shrimp.\n- Sautéing takes \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) minute per shrimp.\n- Five peeled shrimp are discarded, so to sauté \\(n\\) shrimp, she must peel \\(n+5\\).\n\nThe total time is therefore\n\n\\[\n\\frac{n+5}{6}+\\frac{n}{3}\\le 10.\n\\]\n\nMultiplying by 6:\n\n\\[\nn+5+2n\\le 60\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3n\\le 55\n\\]\n\n\\[\nn\\le 18\\frac{1}{3}.\n\\]\n\nThus, she can complete \\(\\boxed{18}\\) shrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To cook 90 usable shrimp, Emily must peel \\(90+5=95\\) shrimp because 5 are discarded.\n\nSince she works sequentially:\n\n- Peeling time:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{95}{6}=15\\frac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\n- Cooking time:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{90}{3}=30\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nTotal time:\n\n\\[\n15\\frac{5}{6}+30=45\\frac{5}{6}\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThus, it will take Emily \\(\\boxed{45\\text{ minutes }50\\text{ seconds}}\\).",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
